  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14201070/assets/a92c3df4f9d410b1a7620cf43b04fda1ce7312cebd8c6077a0b0411ecc78ad73.png)\n\nGiven the quadrilateral above, we have $x=${{field-1}}\n${}^{∘}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the sum of the exterior angles of a polygon is ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2x+(x+{10}^{∘})+(2x-{10}^{∘}) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 6x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={60}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
